<h3><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>3.1 </span><code><span style='font-size:9.5pt'>desktop_app.py</span></code><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>
(The Application Launcher)<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>This
is the first file that runs when the user double-clicks the application.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 1-8: Importing required tools<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import osÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Works with computer files and folders<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import sysÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Accesses Python runtime settings and command line<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import threadingÂ Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Allows running multiple tasks at the exact same time<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import timeÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Handles delays, timestamps, and timeouts<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import tracebackÂ Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Captures full error messages if something crashes<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import urllib.request # Performs internal health check calls to the local server<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import webviewÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Creates the native Microsoft Edge desktop window<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>import uvicornÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># The fast web server engine that runs our backend API</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'> These
standard libraries give Python the power to interact with the Windows OS, run
parallel tasks, and draw a window.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Line 14: Granting automatic microphone permissions<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>os.environ[&quot;WEBVIEW2_ADDITIONAL_BROWSER_ARGUMENTS&quot;] = &quot;--use-fake-ui-for-media-stream --enable-media-stream&quot;</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'> When
a browser accesses a microphone, it usually pops up an annoying <em><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>&quot;Do you want to allow this app
to use your microphone?&quot;</span></em> prompt. This line tells the Edge
Chromium engine: <em><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>&quot;Always
auto-allow the helmet microphone without asking the operator every time.&quot;</span></em><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 69-76: Starting the Backend Web Engine<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>def start_backend_server():<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>uvicorn.run(app, host=&quot;127.0.0.1&quot;, port=8765, log_level=&quot;error&quot;)</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>
Starts the local API server on </span><code><span style='font-size:9.5pt'>127.0.0.1</span></code><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'> (your
local PC) on port </span><code><span style='font-size:9.5pt'>8765</span></code><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 137-144: Opening the Desktop Window<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>window = webview.create_window(<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>title=&quot;Studds QC Testing Dashboard&quot;,<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>url=&quot;http://127.0.0.1:8765/&quot;,<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>width=1100,<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>height=800,<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>resizable=True,<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>js_api=desktop_api<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>)<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span style='font-size:
9.5pt'>webview.start()</span></pre>

