<h3 style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>3.3
</span><code><span style='font-size:9.5pt'>speaker_test.py</span></code><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>
(Stereo Speaker Player)<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Uses
Windows native Multimedia commands (</span><code><span style='font-size:9.5pt'>winmm.dll</span></code><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>) to
play stereo sound cues without opening any external media player.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 22-31: Short-Path Converter<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>def get_short_path_name(long_name: str) -&gt; str:<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â <span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>...<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>res = kernel32.GetShortPathNameW(long_name, buf, 260)</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>
Windows sometimes fails to play audio if folder names have spaces (like </span><code><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>C:\Program Files\Studds</span></code><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>).
This converts paths to 8.3 short format (</span><code><span style='font-size:
9.5pt'>C:\PROGRA~1\Studds</span></code><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>) so playback never fails.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 123-135: Playing the Stereo Audio<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>def start_speaker_test(mp3_path: str) -&gt; Dict[str, Any]:<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>...<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>_mci_send(f'open &quot;{short_path}&quot; type mpegvideo alias speaker_mp3')<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>_mci_send(&quot;play speaker_mp3&quot;)</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'> Opens
the MP3 audio file and starts playback. The audio plays sound strictly in the <strong><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>Left Channel</span></strong> first,
pauses, and then plays strictly in the <strong><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>Right
Channel</span></strong>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

