<h3 style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>3.4
</span><code><span style='font-size:9.5pt'>mic_test.py</span></code><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>
(Offline Speech Recognition Engine)<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Uses
the <strong><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>Vosk Offline Neural
Speech Model</span></strong> to transcribe what the operator says into the
microphone without needing any internet connection.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 94-96: Loading the Neural Speech Model<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>VOSK_MODEL_PATH = os.path.join(get_bundle_dir(), &quot;vosk-model&quot;)<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>speech_model = vosk.Model(VOSK_MODEL_PATH)</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'> Loads
the offline acoustic speech dictionary from the </span><code><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>vosk-model</span></code><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'> folder into memory.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 146-153: Checking for Target Voice Words<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>target_phrases = [&quot;hello studds&quot;, &quot;studds&quot;, &quot;testing&quot;, &quot;hello&quot;]<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>passed = any(phrase in transcript for phrase in target_phrases)<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>return {<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>&quot;status&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot; if passed else &quot;FAIL&quot;,<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>&quot;transcript&quot;: transcript<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>}</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'> When
the operator speaks into the helmet mic, Vosk transcribes the audio. If the
operator says <em><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>&quot;hello
studds&quot;</span></em>, <em><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>&quot;studds&quot;</span></em>,
<em><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>&quot;testing&quot;</span></em>,
or <em><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>&quot;hello&quot;</span></em>,
the test automatically </span><span class=badge-pass1><span style='font-size:
11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>PASSES</span></span><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";color:#24292E'>

<hr size=2 width="100%" align=center>

</span></div>

<h3 style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>3.5
</span><code><span style='font-size:9.5pt'>button_detector.py</span></code><span
style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>
(Physical Button Sensor)<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Listens
for physical button presses on the helmet headset: Volume Up, Volume Down, and
Play/Pause.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 64-66: Key Code Definitions<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>VK_VOLUME_DOWN = 0xAEÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Hardware key code for Volume Down<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>VK_VOLUME_UP = 0xAFÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Hardware key code for Volume Up<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>VK_MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE = 0xB3Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span># Hardware key code for Play/Pause</span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'># Lines 203-214: Volume Change Detection<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>current_volume = volume_ctrl.GetMasterVolumeLevelScalar()<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>if diff &gt; 0.005:<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>button_state[&quot;volume_up&quot;] = True<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>print(&quot;Volume Up detected&quot;)<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>elif diff &lt; -0.005:<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>button_state[&quot;volume_down&quot;] = True<o:p></o:p></span></pre><pre><span
style='font-size:9.5pt'>Â Â Â<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>print(&quot;Volume Down detected&quot;)</span></pre>

<p style='tab-stops:45.8pt 91.6pt 137.4pt 183.2pt 229.0pt 274.8pt 320.6pt 366.4pt 412.2pt 458.0pt 503.8pt 549.6pt 595.4pt 641.2pt 687.0pt 732.8pt'><strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>Explanation:</span></strong><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:#24292E'>
Measures the volume level in real time. If the operator presses Volume (+), the
volume level rises and turns on the green <strong><span style='font-family:
"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>Volume Up</span></strong> badge on screen. If they press
Volume (-), it turns on the green <strong><span style='font-family:"Segoe UI",sans-serif'>Volume
Down</span></strong> badge.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

